# Secret group `settings`: Non-secret paths and tuning shared by several units.
# Loaded by: semprec-api.service, semprec-agents.service, semprec-transcribe.service, semprec-backup.service, semprec-restore-test.service.
#
# Ownership and mode are load-bearing: `root:root 0600`. systemd reads EnvironmentFile= as root
# before dropping privileges. provision.sh installs this template to
# /opt/semprec/shared/env/settings.env only when that file does not exist, so an operator's values are
# never overwritten by a rerun, and it never prints a value. A key belongs to exactly one group
# (docs/adr/2026-10-03-per-service-secret-groups.md); this file is excluded from restic backups.

# FILES_STORAGE_DIR: where uploaded Files blobs are written — by semprec-api (`POST /api/files`,
# served back by `GET /api/blobs/:id`) and semprec-transcribe. Created by provision.sh
# (semprec:semprec, 0750). Required: the services refuse to start without it.
FILES_STORAGE_DIR=/opt/semprec/data/files

# MAIL_ATTACHMENTS_DIR: where semprec-api's mail sync writes mail attachments. Created by
# provision.sh (semprec:semprec, 0750). Required: the api's task list refuses to build without it.
MAIL_ATTACHMENTS_DIR=/opt/semprec/data/mail-attachments

# MinIO is not used: the application writes every blob to FILES_STORAGE_DIR or
# MAIL_ATTACHMENTS_DIR, and the daily backup and monthly restore test cover those two
# directories, not MinIO.

# QUEUE_CONCURRENCY: how many graphile-worker jobs semprec-api and semprec-agents each run at
# once. Ignored by semprec-transcribe, which always runs one job at a time.
QUEUE_CONCURRENCY=4
